00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:05.990 align:start position:0%
the ramsgate futuretown investment plan  sets out a strategy for the town driven  by local people it offers your vision  for the future of ramsgate  this vision is a collaboration that will  be delivered in partnership with local  businesses organizations the community  and a range of public bodies like  historic england and kent county council  the plan was shaped by talking to the  community to find out what is important  to you it hopes to revitalize ramsgate's  economy  address deprivation creating new and  better opportunities for local people  give ramsgate a greater sense of  identity  enable ramsgate to become a place where  people want to live and visit  create a better connected town that  people can walk about  ramsgate is set to benefit from a range  of funding programs including the  levelling up fund high street heritage  action zone and the future high street  funds and this town investment plan will  ensure the money is invested effectively  so local people can see positive changes  in their town  the plan includes projects which funding  has already been secured as well as  outlining significant aspirations for  the future the aim of incorporating  these aspirational projects is to help  leave it in additional grant funding and  investment to support these activities  the plan focuses on four geographical  areas  the first area is the town center local  people think the centre of ramsgate is  neglected unattractive and unwelcoming  the town investment plan sets out an  approach for creating spaces for  businesses to develop and the community  to come together  refurbishing repairing and reactivating  buildings which are not in use  making the town centre a more  environmentally friendly place by  promoting walking and cycling  creating new public spaces is also a  priority  the town centre will be a community and  business hub it will be more active more  attractive and more green  a respondent to the community  questionnaire described the royal  harbour as a jewel in the crown of  planet that needs polishing  projects in this area will protect  retain and secure the future of the  harbour the intention is to improve the  areas where people walk especially along  the waterfront developing the area as a  visitor attraction enhancing the  hospitality offer and creating  opportunities for training and  upskilling local people there will also  be support to help ramsgate's fishermen  and other businesses grow and develop  the port of ramsgate is a key strategic  site and this plan sets out to create a  modern resilient port initiatives such  as the green campus a project to improve  skills and provide quality workspaces  for new green low-carbon businesses  would create a future-facing economy  that benefits ramsgate and creates jobs  for local people tree planting public  realm investment and park and walk  facilities have also been identified to  deliver an inclusive walkable coastal  location where people will want to spend  time  finally eastcliff projects in this area  include the creation of a park along  victoria parade improvements to existing  public spaces and infrastructure  investment in attractions including the  granville theatre and ramsgate tunnels  as well as a new leisure facility the  idea is that eastcliff becomes a  thriving coastal location for residents  and visitors to enjoy  supporting these four geographical areas  is the need for connections so the fifth  strand of the plan is to create a town  that is easy to get around a town that  connects people to amenities and  opportunities this includes better  connecting residential areas such as  newington to the town centre  securing investment across these five  strands has been prioritized to deliver  a ramsgate that is historic resilient  creative inclusive and fun  this video is just an overview of the  ramsgate future town investment plan and  its aspirations you can read the plan in  full find out more and join our mailing  list at ramsgate  future dot co dot uk
 

